          "suppressions": [
            {
              "kind": "external",
              "justification": "The `uploaded_file` parameter originates from `request.FILES['myfile']` in the `upload` view (realvuln-djangoat/app/views/users/benefit_forms/views.py:43), confirming it is attacker-controlled. However, `default_storage.save(full_file_name, content)` at benefits.py:37 uses Django's `FileSystemStorage`, whose `_save()` method calls `self.path(name)` which invokes `safe_join(self.location, name)` (Django 1.11). The `safe_join` utility validates that the resolved path stays within `MEDIA_ROOT` and raises `SuspiciousFileOperation` if it would escape \u2014 this is a real, effective mitigation for CWE-22. The comment \"this way of saving data leaves intended vulnerability\" refers to the manual `os.path.join` construction pattern, but the framework-level guard on the actual file-write path prevents exploitation."
            }
